{"insertText":{"location":{"index":144719,"tabId":"t.l5c18frq5wuo"},"text":"\nAll three models reached ROC-AUC between 0.9878 and 0.9974 on every test set. SwinFusion++ had the highest point estimate of the three on DeeperForensics-1.0 (0.9974) and was within 0.0037 of the highest on the other three test sets (FF++ C23 0.9942, C40 0.9878, Celeb-DF v2 0.9951). In accuracy, it classified the most videos correctly of the three on DeeperForensics-1.0 (397 of 402, compared with 393 for Swin-B and 390 for Video Swin-B) and the second most on Celeb-DF v2 (956 of 978, compared with 933 and 961). On the FaceForensics++ test sets, the three models differed by at most three of 280 videos: SwinFusion++ matched Swin-B on C23 (97.86%) and C40 (94.64%), and Video Swin-B classified three more videos correctly on each. All three models therefore operated near the ceiling of the metric on every test set (ROC curves in Appendix J, Figure J1)."}},
